  "question": {
    "text": "A wedge of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, lying on a rough horizontal plane, is acted upon by a horizontal force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and another force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, inclined at an angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math> to the vertical. The block is in equilibrium, then the minimum coefficient of friction between it and the surface is<br />\r<img src=\"assets\\qt0053_54a1d99bb192.jpg\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 221px;\" />"
  },
